Ques:-

The Nautilus DevOps team has encountered an issue with an EC2 instance named devops-ec2. They are unable to install any packages on this instance due to connectivity issues. The team needs to identify the root cause of the problem and resolve it to restore normal operations.

Investigate the connectivity issue preventing package installation on the EC2 instance devops-ec2.
Implement a solution to resolve the connectivity issue and restore package installation capabilities on the EC2 instance.




Soln:-

Step 1: Identify the Instance and Networking Details

aws ec2 describe-instances --filters "Name=tag:Name,Values=<Instance-name>" \
  --query "Reservations[*].Instances[*].{ID:InstanceId,Subnet:SubnetId,VPC:VpcId,SG:SecurityGroups[*].GroupId}" \
  --output table



Step 2: Check Security Group Rules

aws ec2 describe-security-groups --group-ids <sg-id> \
  --query "SecurityGroups[*].IpPermissions" --output table
  
---->
aws ec2 authorize-security-group-egress --group-id <sg-id> \
  --protocol tcp --port 80 --cidr 0.0.0.0/0

aws ec2 authorize-security-group-egress --group-id <sg-id> \
  --protocol tcp --port 443 --cidr 0.0.0.0/0

  
  
Step3: Check Subnet Route Table

aws ec2 describe-route-tables --filters "Name=association.subnet-id,Values=<subnet-id>" \
  --query "RouteTables[*].Routes" --output table
  


Step 4: Create the Internet Gateway

aws ec2 create-internet-gateway



Step 5: Attach the Internet Gateway to the VPC

aws ec2 attach-internet-gateway --internet-gateway-id <igw-id> --vpc-id <vpc-id>



Step 6: Get the intenet gateway ID along with the filter to check which IGW attached to which VPC

aws ec2 describe-internet-gateways \
  --query "InternetGateways[*].{IGW:InternetGatewayId,VPC:Attachments[*].VpcId}" \
  --output table



Step 7: Command to create the Route Table

aws ec2 create-route-table --vpc-id <vpc-id>



Step 8: Associate the Route Table with a Subnet

aws ec2 associate-route-table --route-table-id <rtb-id> --subnet-id <subnet-id>



Step 9: Add a Default Route to the Internet Gateway

aws ec2 create-route --route-table-id <rtb-id> \
  --destination-cidr-block 0.0.0.0/0 --gateway-id <igw-id>



Step 10: Add the route to the RouteTable

aws ec2 create-route --route-table-id <rtb-id> \
  --destination-cidr-block 0.0.0.0/0 --gateway-id <igw-id>



Step 11: Verify Network ACLs

aws ec2 describe-network-acls --filters "Name=association.subnet-id,Values=<subnet-id>" \
  --query "NetworkAcls[*].Entries" --output table



Step 12: Command to view the NACL ID

aws ec2 describe-network-acls \
  --filters "Name=association.subnet-id,Values=<subnet-id>" \
  --query "NetworkAcls[*].{NACL_ID:NetworkAclId,Subnet:Associations[*].SubnetId}" \
  --output table



